From: WTA301 port <port@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: add monitor_all to keep monitor mode on IPQ5018

Why this patch exists
---------------------
On this board the 5 GHz radio (QCN6122) can do monitor mode but the 2.4 GHz
one (IPQ5018) cannot, and it is not a firmware or configuration problem:

    phy0 (IPQ5018)  Supported interface modes:
                      * managed   * AP   * mesh point
    phy1 (QCN6122)  Supported interface modes:
                      * managed   * AP   * monitor   * mesh point

mac80211 advertises MONITOR unconditionally for every driver
(net/mac80211/main.c:1353, "mac80211 always supports monitor").  ath11k then
takes it away again right after ieee80211_register_hw():

    if (!ab->hw_params.supports_monitor)
            ar->hw->wiphy->interface_modes &= ~BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR);

and core.c has .supports_monitor = false for ATH11K_HW_IPQ5018_HW10 while
ATH11K_HW_QCN9074_HW10 (used by QCN6122) has true.  That is the entire
difference between the two radios.

This patch turns that single removal into something the user can override,
via a module parameter that defaults to off:

    ath11k.monitor_all=0   default, identical to unpatched behaviour
    ath11k.monitor_all=1   keep monitor advertised on IPQ5018 as well

The default matters.  ipq5018's hw_params marks monitor unsupported for a
reason we cannot see from the host side: the Q6 firmware may reject
WMI_VDEV_TYPE_MONITOR for that pdev.  If it does, interface creation fails at
vdev start, which is recoverable (reboot clears the parameter).  Making this
opt-in means nobody gets a different boot behaviour by accident.

Verified on the reference board: phy0 keeps managed/AP/mesh point, phy1 is
unchanged, and the .ko differs from the previous build only in this one
comparison plus the added parameter.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c	2026-11-15 00:48:22.931976063 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c	2026-11-15 00:48:22.963976064 +0800
@@ -35,6 +35,28 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(frame_mode,
 		 "Datapath frame mode (0: raw, 1: native wifi (default), 2: ethernet)");
 
+/*
+ * WTA301: let monitor mode survive on hardware whose hw_params says it is
+ * unsupported.
+ *
+ * mac80211 unconditionally advertises NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR
+ * (net/mac80211/main.c, "mac80211 always supports monitor"), and ath11k then
+ * removes it again after registration when hw_params.supports_monitor is
+ * false.  That flag is false for IPQ5018_HW10, so the 2.4 GHz radio on this
+ * board can never get a monitor interface, while the 5 GHz one can (it uses
+ * the QCN9074 hw_params, where the flag is true).
+ *
+ * Whether the Q6 firmware actually accepts WMI_VDEV_TYPE_MONITOR on that pdev
+ * is not something the host can know, so this is a module parameter that
+ * defaults to off: with monitor_all=0 the behaviour is byte-for-byte what it
+ * was before this patch.
+ */
+bool ath11k_monitor_all;
+module_param_named(monitor_all, ath11k_monitor_all, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(monitor_all,
+		 "Keep monitor mode advertised even if hw_params.supports_monitor is false");
+
+
 bool ath11k_ftm_mode;
 module_param_named(ftm_mode, ath11k_ftm_mode, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(ftm_mode, "Boots up in factory test mode");
